        {
            type: "Raspberry",
            name: "Nova",
            category: "Red raspberry cultivars for Ontario",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "The berries mature 1-2 days after Boyne, are medium-sized, firm, bright, moderately dark.",
            description: "A very productive, early-to-mid-season cultivar, introduced by Agriculture Canada, Kentville, Nova Scotia, in 1980. The berries mature 1-2 days after Boyne, are medium-sized, firm, bright, moderately dark. Flavour is fair. The plant is hardy with erect tall canes with few spines"
